  "source_conclusion": "The existing TestDiskError cluster JUnit passes and reaches the exact named dn0 getBPOSForBlock guard. The v3 keyed map diagnostic records the same object/key put and read, but no map removal or observed typed I/O to null-map path. A pretarget BPServiceActor heartbeat IOException is caught and retried without BlockPoolManager.remove; metadata write IOException aborts the test before transferBlock; later replica file I/O executes after the selected guard. No reviewed existing cluster JUnit plus current typed-I/O fault model changes the null predicate while retaining the selected call. This is a scoped test/fault-model suitability limit, not a claim that production is unreachable or a completed fault campaign.",
